\par\par \b \uc2  Rise In Long Yen Positions Shows Little Fear Of BoJ \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nicholas Hastings \par \uc2 367 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 16:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  LONDON -(Dow Jones)- Speculative players pushed their long positions in the yen to the highest level in more than three years last week, despite continued Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  Although the trend wasn't necessarily being followed by longer-term players, it suggests that the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may struggle to keep the yen at competitive levels. \par \par \uc2  "What they did in January didn't scare away the speculative community," said Paul Mackel, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in London. "I don't think the market is that fearful." \par \par \uc2  Friday the Bank of Japan reported it had spent as much as $4.5 billion on covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during February. This was on top nearly $6 billion spent in January. \par \par \uc2  However, the latest figures from the International Monetary Market in Chicago show speculative players in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures on the Chicago Mercantile Exchange increased their net long yen positions dramatically in the week ended Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Net long positions in the yen against the dollar grew to 35,754 contracts from 18,433 the previous week. Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank, said this increase took them back up to levels last seen in September 1999. \par \par \uc2  While speculators were prepared to raise their short dollar positions against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they were slashing them against the euro and the pound. \par \par \uc2  This reduced the net long euro position sharply to 5,422 from 20,063, the lowest since the end of October last year. \par \par \uc2  "As a consequence it appears that positioning wouldn't impede the upside in the euro below $1.10," said Greg Anderson, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN-Amro in Chicago. Late Monday in Europe, the euro was trading at $1.0807. \par \par \uc2  As far as sterling was concerned, the net speculative position flipped to being net short the pound by 910 contracts after being net long the pound by 376 contracts. However, Anderson suggested that the number of net shorts is probably too small to have any serious influence on market dynamics. \par \par \uc2  -By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030303dz33000yx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
