\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bides time, on Iraq/ \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  watch. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 632 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 14:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, March 3 (Reuters) - The dollar hugged narrow ranges against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as dealers looked ahead to key U.S. manufacturing data and braced for what could be a crucial week for Iraq developments. \par \par \uc2  Baghdad agreed at the weekend to destroy banned missiles and Turkey's parliament blocked a U.S. plan to use the country as a base for a possible attack on Iraq. Some felt this increased the chance of a U.S. assault without broad international backing, which could be the worst case scenario for the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Central banks of Japan, Europe, Britain, Australia, New Zealand, Canada and Norway hold policy-setting meetings this week, with the market pricing in at least a quarter point rate reduction by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "We have an odd situation of very low volatility in the environment of uncertainties. This is because there are negative factors across the board but those pressures are broadly offsetting, while the war issue is still dominating," said Stephen Jen, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Morgan Stanley. \par \par \uc2  "For the U.S., there are negative pressures from the economy and geopolitics but the ECB is about to cut rates, which would be less supportive of European fixed income and the euro." \par \par \uc2  By 1250 GMT the dollar was steady at $1.08 per euro, just over a cent away from a four-year low hit last month. It orbited in a narrow range around 118 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market could remain in suspense until Friday when chief U.N. arms inspector Hans Blix is expected to make another report to the U.N. Security Council. \par \par \uc2  The U.N. said on Monday Iraq would submit a new report on VX nerve gas and anthrax stocks in a week's time. \par \par \uc2  DATA AND RATE DECISION \par \par \uc2  A U.S. manufacturing survey at 1500 GMT will kick off this week's weighty batch of economic data, which includes figures on the U.S. labour market, personal income and spending, and productivity. \par \par \uc2  The Institute of Supply Management index is expected to show growth in U.S. manufacturing slowed in February but remained above the 50 mark separating expansion and contraction. \par \par \uc2  Earlier data showed manufacturing activity in the euro zone stabilised in February. The Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index rose to 50.1 last month from 49.3 in January, beating consensus forecasts. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, analysts said the survey was unlikely to stop the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cutting interest rates this week to shore up business and consumer confidence. \par \par \uc2  "The euro zone PMI figures were better than expected but economic fundamentals still support the case for a rate cut," said Ryan Shea, senior international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  DOLLAR/YEN STALEMATE \par \par \uc2  Dealers were reluctant to sell the dollar aggressively against the yen after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  disclosed last week that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February for a second straight month to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most participants expect the dollar to stay in a tight band against the yen with its downside supported by possible further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities and rises inhibited by geopolitical risks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is keen to curb the yen's strength due to worries that it could harm exports, the main pillar of an economy hobbled by years of deflation. Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it had bought both euros and dollars for yen, although the euro-buying had been "far less". \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan data released on Friday showed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 513 billion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February, compared with 678 billion yen in January. \par \par \uc2  But traders suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and Friday last week, possibly bringing the total amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February close to 1.0 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030303dz3300out\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
