\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar near 1-wk high vs yen on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  news. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 04:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, March 3 (Reuters) - The dollar held firm near a one-week peak against the yen in Asia on Monday morning, still supported by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's revelation that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in February to stem the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  Confirmation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  "by stealth" for a second straight month made traders wary that it might go back into the market should the dollar threaten to fall. \par \par \uc2  "After the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's hard to sell the dollar below 117 yen," said Kota Kimura, assistant manager at Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the greenback was haunted by chances of a U.S.-led war against Iraq, a factor complicated by the Turkish Parliament's refusal to allow the deployment of U.S. troops in its territory near the Iraqi border. \par \par \uc2  As of 0225 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 118.22/25 yen up from 118.09/17 yen in late Friday U.S. trade. It briefly hit a one week-high of 118.29. \par \par \uc2  The euro was also easier versus the dollar at $1.0772/77 compared with $1.0800/06 in U.S. trade last week. \par \par \uc2  It slipped to 127.36/44 yen from 127.62 yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed late on Friday that it had asked the Bank of Japan (BOJ) to step into the market several times in late February. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said it bought both euros and dollars for yen, although the euro-buying had been "far less". \par \par \uc2  "It was a bit of a surprise that they also bought the euro. I think it showed Japan was intent to stop the yen's overall rise, not just rise against the dollar," said Kikuko Takeda, research manager at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "Their latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted after the G7 meeting in late February, also suggests other G7 countries are not opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So that is a relief for the dollar," Takeda said. \par \par \uc2  BOJ data showed Japan spent about 513 billion yen ($4.34 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a month to February 26, compared with 678 billion yen ($5.74 billion) in a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  WAR SEEN INEVITABLE \par \par \uc2  Traders also suspect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and Friday last week, possibly bringing the total amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February close to 1.0 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have sought to curb the yen's strength due to worries that it could harm exports, the main pillar of an economy hobbled by years of deflation. \par \par \uc2  "I think they want to bring the dollar up before any war in Iraq starts, anticipating the dollar will fall when a war breaks out," said Kimura of Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Fear of war against Iraq weighed on the dollar, with many dealers convinced war is inevitable at some point. \par \par \uc2  Such fears, coupled with options-related sales rumoured at 119 yen, were seen as enough to keep the dollar below 119 yen for now, Kimura said. \par \par \uc2  The market showed little reaction to the refusal by Turkey's Parliament on Saturday to permit the deployment of 62,000 American troops in the country, which dealt a blow to U.S. planning for a possible war against Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the market would be unable to move much given huge uncertainty over Iraq ahead of Friday, when chief U.N. arms inspector Hans Blix is expected to make another report to the U.N. Security Council. \par \par \uc2  The United States and Britain are expected to seek U.N backing for war in the form of a resolution by the U.N Security Council in the days after the Blix report, but it is unclear if they have enough support in the 15-member council. \par \par \uc2  For the immediate future, traders are looking to key U.S. data on manufacturers, due at 1500 GMT on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Institute of Supply Management index is expected to show a retreat to 52.4 for February, down from January's 53.9, but still above the 50 mark separating expansion and contraction. \par \par \uc2  Bulls hope a stronger reading could help the dollar but bears are sceptical given that on Friday the dollar failed to capitalise on either better-than-expected fourth-quarter U.S. gross domestic product data or a rise in February's University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey. ($1=118.18 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030303dz330066a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
