\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Account Balance Rose Y513.0B In Feb \b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 11:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account expanded by Y513.0 billion in February, indicating the authorities quietly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets again this month to stem the yen's recent rise. \par \par \uc2  In January, MOF officials confirmed they had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after BOJ data showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account rose Y678.0 billion last month. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants had strongly suspected that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is responsible for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, also sold yen in February through the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  Early this week, when the dollar started sliding on news that Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi had nominated policy conservative Toshihiko Fukui as the next BOJ governor, traders suspected the finance ministry was supporting the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by quietly selling yen in the market. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell Thursday to a six-month low of Y116.85, from around Y120 at the end of January, before staging a one yen rally, which traders attributed to likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But the latest figures, which are based on transaction settlements, don't reflect any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that may have occurred Thursday or Friday, according to a spokesman for the BOJ. \par \par \uc2  In keeping with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest strategy of stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , neither the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or MOF had confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ's figures are included in a table that measures changes in the balances of current accounts at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account reflects transactions between private-sector financial institutions and the account. \par \par \uc2  The data doesn't completely correlate with exact timings of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Finance Ministry and also include \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions related to the government's activities outside Japan such as funding for embassies. \par \par \uc2  The last sizable net increase in the BOJ's figures before January occurred last year in May, June and July - around the same time as the MOF's stated market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In those months, the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account at the BOJ rose by Y1.06 trillion, Y2.27 trillion and Y520.5 billion respectively. \par \par \uc2  -By Asako Tanabe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; asako.tanabe@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030228dz2s000nv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
