\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ Data To Confirm Japan Sold Yen In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Mkt In February \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 04:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this month, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  data to be released Friday evening are all but sure to show. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry has been quietly selling yen almost every day this week to curb the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise as the dollar tumbled amid heightening geopolitical uncertainties, financial sources close to the government say. \par \par \uc2  While finance ministry officials have refused to confirm or deny the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  through repeated "no comments," they have stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves over the past week have been "rapid" - a word they often use to justify taking action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "We are aware of the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, or the yen's rise, from the end of last week to this week have been rapid," Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the ministry's International Bureau told reporters late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Our stance remains unchanged in that we will take action against rapid movements which don't reflect fundamentals," he added. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, Watanabe's boss and top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  point man, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi ventured further, saying that he couldn't talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  while "in the middle of things," noting that "there are various ways to act" in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  In any case, BOJ data of money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for February, to be released around 1000 GMT, are expected to make clear the fact the government has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The data will show roughly how much the finance ministry spent selling yen, although it will be unclear whether it sold yen only for dollars, or also for euros. \par \par \uc2  Based on local money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  done by the BOJ every day, analysts estimate the MOF sold a combined total of around Y400 billion-Y500 billion Tuesday and Wednesday to cap the yen's surge. The ministry also likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Last month, after similar data forced their hand, finance ministry officials confirmed they had sold Y700 billion for dollars to prop up the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded as low as Y116.85 in the past week. At 0310 GMT it was changing hands around Y117.65, down from a high for the week of Y118.80 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Alastair Gale \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030228dz2s00065\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
