\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2  news pounds yen vs euro, dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Justyna Pawlak \par \uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The yen sank versus the euro and the dollar on Friday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  a few times this month against the country's stubbornly strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The euro was the main beneficiary of the market's yen-beating after Japan revealed it had been buying euros as well as dollars, even though it typically is more concerned with the yen's strength against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  news was more muted as markets awaited world powers' responses to the latest United Nations arms inspectors' findings on Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Data showed the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the finance ministry's behalf, had spent about 513 billion yen ($4.36 billion) in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the yen's rise in February after selling 678 billion yen in January. \par \par \uc2  "It is a bit surprising that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not increase the size of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Michael Metcalfe, senior strategist at State Street in London. "They will have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in larger sizes to get the dollar back above 120 yen." \par \par \uc2  "We have seen a bigger move in euro/yen than dollar/yen because Japan decided to go through the euro also," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 1300 GMT on Friday, the yen was down 0.4 percent on the dollar\par since late Thursday, trading at 118.05. It was down 0.74 percent on the\par euro at 127.30           .\par The single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , meanwhile, was up a third of a percent versus the\par greenback at $1.0785. The dollar had reversed earlier losses against\par sterling  but remained weaker versus the Swiss franc       .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DOUBTS ON JAPAN\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say weakening the yen is an uphill battle for Japan which\par frets that a rapid rise in its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could damage its economy by\par hurting export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But with Japan running a large current account surplus, the yen has\par strong support from local corporates as well as hedging and\par repatriation by domestic money managers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I am sceptical about Japan's ability to forestall a move back to\par levels we have tested yesterday," said Derek Halpenny, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par economist at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in London.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The embattled dollar probed a six month low near 116.80 yen on Thursday\par as traders increasingly viewed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent tactics of covert\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as failing to scare off flows into yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Speculative dollar-selling is easier to turn off with \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par but yen-buying can only be slowed down," said Halpenny.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MISSILE PLANS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the geopolitical front, Washington dismissed Baghdad's agreement to\par destroy its al-Samoud 2 missiles and pressed on with its war\par preparations.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Iraq said missile destruction could begin on Saturday in line with U.N.\par demands that it dismantles conventional weapons beyond its permitted\par range, but both Washington and the UK were sceptical that Baghdad was\par using delay tactics to avert war.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UK Prime Minister Tony Blair told Iraqi President Saddam Hussein "this\par is not a time for games," in reaction to the missile disposal pledge.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, a leaked report by UN arms inspector Hans Blix, in which he\par called Iraqi cooperation on arms inspections problematic, is expected\par to reach UN Security Council members over the weekend. Blix is due to\par address the council at the end of next week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The council remains deeply divided with its first meeting since the\par introduction of a U.S.-UK-Spanish resolution to lay the legal\par groundwork for war, erupting into chaos on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It's the same old story," said Steven Pearson, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland treasury services in London.\par "People are trying to ascertain what Hans Blix's comments mean for the\par potential for war."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bearish comments from top policy officials and disappointing data\par releases continued to underscore the grim economic outlook for the euro\par zone on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par European Union Economic and Monetary Affairs Commissioner Pedro Solbes\par said during a visit to Budapest that 2003 economic growth in the euro\par zone was likely to be lower than the 1.8 percent forecast issued by the\par European Commission in November.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Furthermore, euro zone sentiment surveys showed consumer and business\par confidence slightly down to steady this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par January's consumer inflation came out at 2.2 percent and preliminary\par estimates put it at 2.3 percent this month, still above the European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's two percent target ceiling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Across the Atlantic, U.S. fourth quarter growth figures at 1330 GMT are\par expected to show the world's largest economy grew one percent in the\par final quarter of 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Chicago purchasing managers' report is due at 1500 GMT and expected\par to show a reading of 53 versus 56 in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030228dz2s00qux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
