\par\par \b \uc2  Euro gains on yen,aided by  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention \highlight\uc2  news. \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The euro extended its gains on the yen on Friday, boosted by confirmation from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February by buying euros and dollars to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro had climbed half a percent up on the day to session highs at 127.22 yen  by 1100 GMT and its gains against the yen also gave it a leg up against the dollar to stand a third of a percent up at $1.0786     . \par \par \uc2  "It's the fact they confirmed how much they did and against what \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  (which is helping the euro)," said a trader at a Japanese bank in London \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 513 billion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February compared with 678 billion yen in January, Bank of Japan data showed on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry confirmed that it had asked the BOJ to step into the market a few times in late February and that it bought both dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a six-month low of 116.80 yen  on Thursday, despite talk in the market the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have been in during the session. The dollar was at 117.88 yen by 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030228dz2s00m2i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
