\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  confirms  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2  in Feb. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed on Friday that it had conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second straight month in February to stem the yen's rise, which authorities fear could hurt exports. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 513 billion yen in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February compared with 678 billion yen in January, Bank of Japan data showed. \par \par \uc2  The Finance Ministry confirmed that it had asked the BOJ to step into the market a few times in late February and that it bought both dollars and euros, but euro-buying had been "far less" than dollar-buying versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen has been probing six-month highs against the dollar this week despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  discreetly is losing its potency. \par \par \uc2  "This is the second time they said they were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  so it's not a surprise any more," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at J.P. Morgan Chase. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is losing its effect on the market." \par \par \uc2  The ministry said Japan acted alone and that the aim was to control volatility in the market. \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb market volatility stemming from speculative moves amid continued uncertainty over geopolitical risks," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) source said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data, covering the period up to Wednesday, showed the Finance Ministry paid 513 billion yen to the private sector through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data covers settlements from January 30 to February 26. The MOF source declined to say whether \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place on February 27. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as agent for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  EURO/YEN \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Dealers had said they had detected the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late last week as the dollar dropped below 119 yen. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, it dropped to 116.85 yen, its lowest in nearly six months, on growing nervousness over a looming war in Iraq and signs of weakness in the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  That was down about four percent from this year's high of 121.78 yen hit about two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 117.83/88 yen at 1134 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The MOF source said the ministry would continue to monitor the euro as well as the dollar and would act on either \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "when we see it as necessary, judging from the relative fundamentals of the three \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  The last time Japan bought euros for yen was on June 28, 2002. \par \par \uc2  The euro, which had stood above 130 yen just two week ago, has been under strong downward pressure. It dropped to a one-month low of around 126 yen this week. \par \par \uc2  The euro's drop was a key factor adding downward pressure to the dollar/yen rate, which could have disturbed the Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in euro/yen was because they realised that position-unwinding by people who had been long euros and short yen was propelling the yen across the board," said Toshiyuki Suzuki, senior economist at UFJ Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  "If we continue to see large fluctuations, the authorities are likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  like this again," he added. \par \par \uc2  TECHNICAL LEVELS \par \par \uc2  The MOF source said he had the impression that upward market pressure on the yen had strengthened since mid-February. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to be conducted in such a way as to prevent the yen rising beyond technically important points at 116.82 yen against the dollar and 126 yen against the euro, as the yen's rise was expected pick up speed if those levels were broken. \par \par \uc2  "Although the yen is the weakest fundamentally, the market wants to sell the dollar as geopolitical worries and fading confidence in the U.S. economy are putting big pressure on the dollar," a senior fund manager at a Japanese bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Without fresh policies in conjunction with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as further monetary easing, I don't think the Japanese authorities can really alter the present downward trend of the dollar against the yen," the fund manager said. \par \par \uc2  Japan has been selling its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1999 and the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase Japanese external reserves, which were already at a record high of $478.593 billion at the end of January, more than twice as high as in January 1999. \par \par \uc2  During the period between 1999 and 2002, Japan sold the yen against the dollar and the euro on 32 days. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030228dz2s00ld6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
