\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up vs yen but Iraq and BOJ lock it in range. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 652 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2003\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 28 (Reuters) - The dollar regained some ground on the yen on Friday on talk Japan had sneaked into the market to sell yen but business was muted as traders awaited world powers' responses to the latest UN arms inspectors' findings on Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan, which acts as the Japanese Finance Ministry's agent, had been detected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly since late last week and was thought to have bought dollars up to 117.50-117.60 yen on Thursday, market sources said. While Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Friday he did not think the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders were awaiting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data around 1000 GMT for evidence of BOJ activity. \par \par \uc2  According to a draft Security Council report, chief U.N. weapons inspector Hans Blix criticized Iraq for a "very limited" response to its disarmament obligations, even as Baghdad agreed in principle to start destroying missiles the UN deems illegal. \par \par \uc2  "The main issues are whether and where the BOJ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the dollar against the yen and how the weapons inspections process is going to bear out for prospects of war in the Gulf," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland treasury services. \par \par \uc2  All this was keeping the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  locked in tight ranges. By 0855 GMT, the dollar was almost unchanged from late New York levels at 117.61 yen, after touching a six-month low of 116.80 in Thursday's trading session. \par \par \uc2  It was softer on the day on the euro at $1.0760 and the safe-haven Swiss franc at 1.3593. \par \par \uc2  CAT AND MOUSE \par \par \uc2  After Japan said in late January it had surreptitiously sold 678 billion yen to dampen its export-damaging strength, traders are awaiting BOJ data that will confirm whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the month to Wednesday, and if so, how much it spent. \par \par \uc2  "The point to look out for is whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more or less than last time," said a senior analyst at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  "But even if we learn that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily, it's very tough for the authorities to reverse the dollar's current downtrend," he said. \par \par \uc2  "At the most, Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can only afford to buy time, while now the dollar is more vulnerable with the geopolitical factor and signs of weakness in the U.S. economy." \par \par \uc2  On the geopolitical front, Washington dismissed Baghdad's agreement to destroy its al-Samoud 2 missiles and pressed on with its war preparations. \par \par \uc2  Blix's report, leaked on Thursday, is expected to reach UN Security Council members over the weekend and he is then due to address the council at the end of next week. \par \par \uc2  However the council remains deeply divided with its first meeting since the introduction of a U.S.-UK-Spanish resolution to lay the legal groundwork for war erupting into chaos on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It's the same old story,"said Pearson. "People are trying to ascertain what Hans Blix's comments mean for the potential for war. The market at the moment is taking it as potentially Iraq will make concessions to avoid a conflict." \par \par \uc2  A raft of data is due later, with a first euro zone inflation estimate for February, at 1100 GMT, forecast to show consumer price inflation running at 2.2 percent year on year, above the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2.0 percent target ceiling. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone business and consumer sentiment surveys are due at the same time, while U.S. fourth quarter growth figures at 1330 GMT are expected to show the world's largest economy grew one percent in the final quarter of 2002. \par \par \uc2  The Chicago purchasing managers' report is scheduled for 1500 GMT and expected to show a reading of 53.0 compared with 56.0 in January. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030228dz2s00iua\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
