\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar Leaps On More Suspicion Of Quiet BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry and Agnes T. Crane \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2003\par 16:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar got a burst of adrenaline Thursday, shooting higher against the yen in a move that appeared to confirm traders' suspicions that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  Although the greenback's advance - also driven by some hope that Iraq might make new concessions to U.N. weapons inspectors and hence avert a war - was fairly broad based, it was against the yen that the dollar showed most strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar jumped to Y117.62, up Y116.85 around midday in London and from Y117.13 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, reached Thursday night in Tokyo, declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation. \par \par \uc2  Proof of the pudding should come Friday in Asia when the Bank of Japan is slated to release statistics that should show whether or not \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past month to push the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  That's what happened in January, when the BOJ - which acts on the MOF's behalf in such \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - sold some $6 billion worth of yen in covert \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it only declared after the event. This stealth approach was a break with tradition and has made \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders increasingly nervous that the BOJ may be in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market covertly since. \par \par \uc2  Two \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders consulted in New York for this report said they suspected the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of some $2 billion during Thursday's global trading session, starting in Asia and continuing into the European, then New York trading sessions. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said they haven't actually seen BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  take place, however. But they did cite a rising tide of market speculation that the BOJ is behind the bid for dollars against yen among different types of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants. \par \par \uc2  Japan is desperately keen to avoid letting a strong yen derail an extremely fragile recovery in the world's second largest economy. \par \par \uc2  Among the indications that the BOJ's hand may be at work driving the yen lower Thursday were bids from some Japanese commercial banks in the order of $2 billion to buy dollars against yen, said Thomas Molloy, a trader at Bank Leumi. \par \par \uc2  The size of such orders exceeded the usual magnitude of a bid from some of these banks, had they been buying on their own behalf. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese bid interest is not for themselves," but for some bigger, third party, he said. \par \par \uc2  Some others emphasized their continuing suspicion from earlier sessions this week that Japanese commercial banks may be not acting under orders from the BOJ, but attempting to front run an admission of official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  they expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to make. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese banks normally have the good oil: that's a  good indication there may be something coming through," said one New York-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist. \par \par \uc2  A senior Japanese finance ministry official warned Thursday the yen's rise over the past week has been rapid, but declined to say whether his ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent days to curb the rise. \par \par \uc2  "We are aware of the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements, or the yen's rise, from the end of last week to this week have been rapid," said Hiroshi Watanabe, head of the ministry's International Bureau. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par    By Agnes Crane; Dow Jones Newswires\par    agnes.crane@dowjones.com; 201-938-2248\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030227dz2r005k2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
