\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-BOJ bought dollars around 117 yen on Tuesday-sources. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2003\par 04:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 26 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday, buying dollars for yen in the latest leg of a campaign to stem the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, market sources said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They said the Bank of Japan, which acts as an agent of the Finance Ministry, was detected to have stepped in to buy dollars at around 117.00-117.20 yen in late Asian time and during post-Asian trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Since late last week, the market has been abuzz with rumours that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had conducted covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The rumours were fuelled by the knowledge that the Japanese government stepped in to sell yen covertly in late January during a period of rapid yen strengthening. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been made through a greater number of banks, including several foreign ones. \par \par \uc2  One market source said that the amount of the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be substantial. \par \par \uc2  "Not only on Tuesday, but (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is believed to have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  almost every day recently," said a bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "This time, the market talk is that the MOF (Finance Ministry) is using some foreign banks for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well as some Japanese banks." \par \par \uc2  The yen was trading at around 117.46/49 yen at Wednesday midday, down from a six-month high against the dollar of 117.00 yen in post-Asian trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Hit by fears of a looming war in Iraq, the dollar is down nearly four percent since hitting a high of 121.78 yen about two weeks ago. \par \par \uc2  On January 31, Japan revealed that it had quietly bought $6.0 billion from mid-January to stem the yen's rise, but its recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have done little more than give the dollar a temporary respite. \par \par \uc2  Between April and June last year, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record amount on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , forking out four trillion yen ($34 billion) to sap the yen's strength. That time, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed its act shortly after conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar's drop was triggered by Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, who said on Tuesday that Group of Seven ministers meeting last weekend had agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be determined by the market. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers took his comments to mean that Japan would not get much help from its G7 partners in its efforts to slow the yen's export-damaging advance. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Japanese authorities tried to played down such speculation by keeping up their threats, saying they were ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if necessary. \par \par \uc2  Top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi said recent movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been rapid and inappropriate, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  was watching the market closely. \par \par \uc2  "Recents movements have been rapid. The yen has moved about four yen against the dollar in a week," Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "Such movements are inappropriate, and the ministry is closely watching against excessive movements," he added. \par \par \uc2  He declined to say if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Separately, a senior official at the ministry said that Shiokawa's comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates did not indicate any change in the ministry's stance. \par \par \uc2  ($1=117.45 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030226dz2q006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
