\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rallies on Shiokawa  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  remarks. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 791 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2003\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The yen rallied to its highest level against the dollar in nearly six months on Tuesday after Japan's finance minister said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be left to market forces. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said G7 ministers meeting last weekend in Paris had agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should be determined by the market, comments dealers took to imply that Japan would not get much help in its efforts to slow the yen's export-damaging advance. \par \par \uc2  The yen rose as high as 117 per dollar , its highest level since early September 2002. \par \par \uc2  In a bit of damage control, Shiokawa later said the Japanese government would continue to respond to rapid or speculative moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "You can't dismiss the short-term impact of Shiokawa's remarks," said Bob Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in New York. "Still, they don't preclude the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  from ordering the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Indeed, there was talk on Tuesday that the Bank of Japan was on the bid at 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ earlier this month confirmed that it had quietly sold yen for dollars in January to slow the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advance, and rumors of further stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have cropped up from time to time in the past few weeks. \par \par \uc2  By late afternoon in New York, the dollar was trading at 117.26 yen, a half percent decline on the session. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was off 0.90 percent at 126.12 yen , near session lows of 126.06. \par \par \uc2  "There was a good (yen) rally off of 127.40 yen on the Shiokawa news ... That doesn't bode well for euro/yen or dollar/yen,' said Enrico Caruso, chief dealer at Temple Asset Management in Los Angeles. He noted that Japanese investors have been heavy sellers of European assets ahead of the Japanese fiscal year-end on March 31. \par \par \uc2  The euro's sharp fall against the yen also helped to take it down a notch versus the dollar. The euro was at $1.0757 in late U.S. dealings , down 0.36 percent on the session. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was up 0.18 percent versus the Swiss franc to 1.3574 francs . \par \par \uc2  It was the second day of sharp gains for the yen. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied on Monday on views the government's choice for new BOJ governor, Toshihiko Fukui, was unlikely to champion yen-weakening steps such as inflation-targeting or massive buying of foreign bonds. \par \par \uc2  The yen's rally was muted somewhat by news that North Korea had test fired one or more land-to-ship missiles. \par \par \uc2  Concern over a war in Iraq also remained very much in focus for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. U.S. President George W. Bush on Tuesday emphasized his intention to bypass the United Nations and attack Iraq if necessary. \par \par \uc2  NO CONFIDENCE \par \par \uc2  The dollar suffered a short-lived setback on news that U.S. consumer sentiment dived in February. \par \par \uc2  Consumer confidence as reported by the Conference Board, a private research group, fell sharply and unexpectedly to the lowest level in nearly 10 years as Americans fretted about the increasing threat of war with Iraq, weak stock markets and rising oil prices. \par \par \uc2  The reading of 64.0 was nearly 15 points lower than January's levels and well below economists' expectations of 76.8. \par \par \uc2  The bleak sentiment report was in sharp contrast to a better-than-expected reading on Germany's business climate, as measured by the closely watched Ifo index. \par \par \uc2  The index rose to 88.9 in February from 87.4 in January, way ahead of expectations and its highest level in seven months. The Munich-based Ifo reported an improvement in both current conditions and expectations. \par \par \uc2  The bad news in the U.S. confidence report was tempered by news that housing starts rose 0.2 percent in January to the highest rate since mid-1986. \par \par \uc2  "The decline in consumer confidence is an issue, but until you see a dramatic slowdown in consumption, it probably won't be a huge problem for the dollar,' said BNP Paribas' Lynch. \par \par \uc2  The data calendar is light on Wednesday, but both Germany and the U.K. will release fourth-quarter 2002 growth data. \par \par \uc2  In other trading on Tuesday, sterling tumbled to a four-year low of 68.63 pence per euro  after the Bank of England's top economist said Britain's current account deficit may require a further drop in the British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  It was trading at 68.33 pence per euro in late New York dealings, a gain of half a percent for the euro. Against the dollar, sterling was off 0.86 percent at $1.5757 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030226dz2p00025\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
