\par\par \b \uc2  Hayami calls  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to weaken yen 'useless'. \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2003\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 25 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said on Tuesday that trying to weaken the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was useless, but small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth the market could be appropriate. \par \par \uc2  "Given \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (strong economic) potential, the yen may weaken temporarily through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it will come back. So \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen would be completely useless," he told a private seminar. But he said dollar buying after the September 11 attacks was appropriate, as were small amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He also said it would not be possible to weaken the yen to 150 yen to the dollar - a rate cited by Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, who said that was based on purchasing power parity. \par \par \uc2  Hayami is to step down at the end of his five-year term as governor on March 19. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Policy Board will hold its last regular policy-setting meeting under his leadership on March 4-5. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030225dz2p009ez\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
