\par\par \b \uc2  Shiokawa:Watching  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , May Need To Show Aggressive Stance \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2003\par 00:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- In a stern warning that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets after the yen surged overnight, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Tuesday that authorities might need to "show an aggressive stance." \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell a yen overnight as market participants priced in Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's nomination of conservative Toshihiko Fukui to take over as Bank of Japan governor next month, a move that dashed expectations for a radical easing by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its fight against deflation. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa attributed the yen's strength to broader trends in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was getting squeezed higher by movements in the dollar and the euro. \par \par \uc2  "As the dollar-euro relationship is moving, Japan needs to think of a proper way to balance this," Shiokawa told reporters after a Cabinet meeting. \par \par \uc2  "While watching (the markets), we may need to show an aggressive stance," he added, hinting at possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the yen. \par \par \uc2  At 0203 GMT Tuesday, the euro was trading around $1.0787 after rising overnight. It has strengthened against the dollar as war fears have deterred dollar buying. \par \par \uc2  Selling of the dollar/euro pair has also helped weaken the value of the greenback against the yen. The dollar fell against the yen overnight in New York as a potential war against Iraq appeared to draw closer. \par \par \uc2  At 0203 GMT Tuesday, the dollar was trading around Y117.88 after jumping as high as Y118.20 on reports earlier in the morning that North Korea Monday fired a missile that landed in the sea between the Korean Peninsula and Japan. \par \par \uc2  -By James Simms, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; james.simms@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Hugh Lawson and Bennett Richardson \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030224dz2o001fk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
