\par\par \b \uc2  GLOBAL YIELD: BOJ Musical Chairs But Japan Song The Same \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 1,066 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2003\par 21:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- A decidedly unadventurous choice for the new Bank of Japan governor has dispelled illusions that Japan is set to take an aggressive approach to fight deflation, which somewhat ironically lifted the yen Monday. \par \par \uc2  But over the medium term, the selection will both weigh on the yen and keep Japanese assets as a whole trapped in the quandary that has plagued the world's second biggest economy for more than a decade. "It's a classic Japanese compromise really," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research with Mellon Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  After months of speculation, Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi selected former Bank of Japan Deputy Governor Toshihiko Fukui to replace outgoing BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, asking the ruling coalition to begin procedures for securing his appointment in the Diet. \par \par \uc2  The choice was a disappointment for those buying into Koizumi's oft-repeated mantra that he wanted a dedicated deflation fighter from the private sector at the helm of the BOJ. In the end, he chose an establishment candidate who is little different from the incumbent, only firming a sense of cynicism surrounding any reform efforts in the world's second largest economy. \par \par \uc2  "It's the same old stuff," where Japan's policy makers aren't likely to take drastic measures in an effort to wrest the economy out of its long running deflationary spiral, Gunner said. \par \par \uc2  Among the few strategies the BOJ can employ in a bid to weaken the yen, with its short term interest rates already effectively at zero, is to ramp up purchases of Japanese government bonds, injecting more money into the financial system, which would automatically weaken the yen. But the initial impression that Fukui may not favor aggressive moves to do so, possibly resisting policy makers at the government, has helped to drive the dollar a full yen lower against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "His selection is a major disappointment for those hoping that the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head would crank up the printing presses to tackle deflation," said David Mozina, head of G10 strategy with Banc of America Securities in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Radical reflation would have driven the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower," Mozina added. "Preservation of the status quo, therefore, removes a big negative for the yen." \par \par \uc2  Former BOJ policy board member Nobuyuki Nakahara, an avid proponent of monetary easing whose appointment would have signaled yen weakness, was the other leading contender for the job. But analysts reckon his appointment would have encountered stiff opposition from within Koizumi's ruling Liberal Democratic Party. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Raising \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chances\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Now, the firming of the yen, which threatens to snuff out any\par prospects of an export-led recovery, raises the chances of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par finance ministry stepping in to undertake \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , strategists warned. The MOF acts via the Bank of Japan in such\par moves.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After the BOJ revealed that it had undertaken covert \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par weaken the yen last month, traders are already jumpy at the prospect of\par a repeat performance, especially as the dollar has fallen below the key\par Y118.0 on  Monday. The greenback is already at roughly the same levels\par where the BOJ was thought to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Now, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could occur "at any moment," warned Robert Sinche,\par chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with Citibank in New York. The question on\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders minds' is already  whether the Y117.0 area would offer\par any support for the dollar, or whether it will fall through that over\par the next two global trading sessions, Sinche said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But over the longer term, the yen is expected to weaken of its own\par accord, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market participants return to focus on the\par woes of Japan's economy and ailing banking system, especially once the\par habitual flurry of repatriation into yen assets ahead of the country's\par fiscal year end on Mar. 31 peters out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prices of some other key Japanese asset markets may also  take a turn\par for the worse. Most notably, dangers lurk in the Japanese government\par bond market, where yields aren't far off the record lows they plumbed in\par January. The 10-year JGB's yield - which moves inversely to its price -\par was at 0.82% Monday in New York, down two basis points from Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The JGB market's virtual shrug at Fukui's nomination may have been\par partly because of flows into Japanese assets ahead of the fiscal year\par end supporting JGBs, and the pivotal role by domestic investors who hold\par some 95% of JGBs outstanding.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par These domestic investors include banks, who have little choice but to\par park funds where they can collect returns, albeit at a a pitifully low\par level, given the stagnation of their core lending business amid a feeble\par economic environment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Still Risks In JGBs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nonetheless, JGB prices are precariously high, many U.S. based bond\par strategists agree. Even should Japanese policy makers be partially\par successful over the longer term in introducing some pricing pressures\par into the Japanese economy, that could wreak serious damage to JGBs,\par warns Lee Thomas, head of global bond strategy with PIMCO, the world's\par biggest bond fund.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There is some chance that the two deputy governors of the BOJ,\par appointed along with Fukui, will manage to fight the government's corner\par to a degree in pushing for some new measures to generate pricing\par pressures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The two - Kazumasa Iwata and Toshiro Mutoh - may work on the\par government's behalf and in so doing create "a much more volatile, open\par discussion about what will be needed at the BOJ now," said Gunner. This\par could raise the volume of "dissenting voices wanting an inflation\par target," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Yet a more damaging factor that may weigh on JGB prices depends not so\par much on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but on the government's political will and\par ability to push through drastic structural reforms aimed at forcing the\par nation's ailing banks to aggressively write off bad loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par According to Goldman Sachs' estimate made last year, Japanese banks'\par bad debts and nonperforming loans totaled a huge Y236 trillion. If these\par reform efforts continue to get watered down, that ultimately may force\par the government to ramp up debt issuance in order to bail out creditors\par of tottering banks, denting JGB prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030224dz2o0080x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
