\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar firmer in Asia after G7, BOJ head watched. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 617 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2003\par 00:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The dollar was firmer in early Asia on Monday after Group of Seven (G7) finance ministers and central bankers gave no surprising remarks about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements but said they would cooperate closely on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Repeating the G7's standard line on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, their final statement said: "We will continue to monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as necessary." \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Tokyo said there was no surprise in the G7 communique, but that the dollar was unlikely to be sold off for the time being as the group did not seem to have criticised \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's covert \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted last month. \par \par \uc2  "There was no surprise from the G7 meeting. It showed their stance to cooperate closely and it seems that there was no particular opinion opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Shigetake Nakayama, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing at UFJ Bank. \par \par \uc2  "As position adjustment to sell the euro against the dollar is taking place this morning, I expect the dollar to test its upside for the time being," he said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said he did not talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates when he met his U.S. counterpart. \par \par \uc2  U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow reiterated that a strong dollar remains in the best interests of the United States. \par \par \uc2  French Finance Minister Francis Mer said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are operating as normal and there was no risk at the moment of any uncontrolled developments. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 118.83/91 yen in early Asia, up from about 118.30 yen around this time in Asia on Friday and from the late U.S. level of 118.64/72 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar is likely to test 119.20/30 in the near term due to ongoing position adjustment to sell euros against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro fell in early Asia to as low as around $1.0715 after stop-loss sales were triggered around $1.0750. It now stands at $1.0724/28. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also drew support from a rise in major U.S. stock indexes on Friday as investors were cheered by the possibility war could be averted. An Iraqi official said Baghdad was "ready for dialogue with the American administration to build economic ties and cooperation" should the U.S. drop plans to invade Iraq. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the possibility of a U.S.-led invasion of Iraq remains, and this will keep the dollar in a weak position for the time being. "As long as the Iraq situation is not cleared up, I don't think the dollar will have clear direction," said Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  FUKUI AS BOJ HEAD? \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar's upside was also expected to be weighed down by a media report that former Bank of Japan official Toshihiko Fukui was likely to be the next \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head. \par \par \uc2  The Yomiuri newspaper reported on Monday that final talks are under way to appoint Fukui, who is considered a conservative candidate, to replace current Governor Masaru Hayami, whose five-year term ends on March 19. \par \par \uc2  BOJ watchers consider 67-year-old Fukui, now head of Fujitsu Research Institute, as unlikely to depart from the policies pursued by Hayami, an opponent of inflation targeting. \par \par \uc2  "The report could weigh on the dollar but I expect a limited effect as investors, especially foreign funds, have already been pushing down the dollar from 120 yen on the possibility of Fukui's appointment," Hanao said. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi is expected to announce his decision on a replacement for Hayami in the next few days. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030223dz2n00vy1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
