\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar still fragile - market ponders G7. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Mariko Hayashibara \par \uc2 749 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 03:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The dollar held above a three-week low against the yen in Thursday morning Asian trade on Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats, but struggled to gain amid a re-emergence of war risks and ahead of a weekend Group of Seven meeting. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said on Thursday there is no change in the Finance Ministry's stance that it will act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We have seen some rapid moves recently. We believe that such rapid ups and downs are not appropriate," Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly to weaken the yen in late January, and many wonder whether such action will be discussed at the G7 meeting in Paris this weekend. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said earlier this week that the dollar/yen exchange rate would not be a topic when he meets his U.S. counterpart on the sidelines of the G7 talks. \par \par \uc2  But the U.S. Treasury undersecretary for international affairs, John Taylor, said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely feature in discussions in meetings of finance ministers, though they would not be the main focus of the talks. \par \par \uc2  This apparently contradicted statements by Japanese and Canadian officials that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be on the G7 agenda. \par \par \uc2  "I think the United States seems very critical of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the U.S. wants transparency and the announcement effect when conducting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Toru Umemoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "And as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted before the G7 meeting, I think it's impossible for Japan not to give an explanation to the United States," he added. \par \par \uc2  "It's very odd that Japan's Finance Ministry is saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue won't be on the agenda while the U.S. side is saying it will be discussed," Umemoto said. \par \par \uc2  Umemoto and others said if the U.S. makes any negative comment this weekend about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it would likely push up the yen, possibly to near 115 yen. \par \par \uc2  By 0226 GMT, the dollar was trading at 118.81/86 yen, compared to 118.70 in late New York trade but not far from a three-week low of 118.57 yen hit overnight. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN REPATRIATION, IRAQ \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0760/63, up slightly from $1.0745 and at 127.85/94 yen from 127.55. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders have been sensitive to euro/yen moves after huge positions were unloaded earlier this week mainly from foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese investors, depending on where domestic stocks are trading at the beginning of March, will need to take profits in something before March book-closings (for the end of Japan's financial year), and that could well be in euro-denominated assets," said a trader at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro touched three-week lows of around 126.84 yen earlier this week, holding the 38.2 percent retracement support from its rise from November. The focus now is on whether it will retest that low to give way to the 50-percent retracement around 125.50. \par \par \uc2  Such pressure in the euro against the yen was weighing indirectly on the dollar/yen rate. \par \par \uc2  Investors have also sold the dollar on concerns that the United States could launch a unilateral military offensive against Iraq without the sanction of the United Nations. \par \par \uc2  Those fears have been amplified as Washington has tried without success to win the backing of reluctant allies for military action. \par \par \uc2  Data on Wednesday showing the U.S. housing sector remaining buoyant in January failed to help both Wall Street and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dealers and analysts said there was growing speculation among Japanese market participants that former Bank of Japan Deputy Governor Toshihiko Fukui may be appointed next governor of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last week, the yen weakened as Takatoshi Ito, a Tokyo University professor and an outspoken advocate of inflation targeting, was seen as a front-runner candidate. \par \par \uc2  Ito is scheduled to speak at a forum on inflation targeting hosted by the Cabinet Office's research arm, which starts at 0500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Politics experts are saying that Ito would not speak loudly in public at this time if he was really to be the next BOJ governor," Morgan Stanley's Umemoto said. \par \par \uc2  "And if Fukui is the one, I think the yen will be bought back further," Umemoto said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030220dz2k00vmy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
