\par\par \b \uc2  ODJ Traders Fear Covert  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  May Be Braking Yen Rise \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry and Tyler Lifton \par \uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 18:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The suspicion that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be\par covertly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets is helping to support the dollar\par against the yen Thursday morning in New York, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders and strategists\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This shadow of a doubt that the Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of the\par finance ministry, may be actively involved in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to\par weaken the yen, is being stoked by the fact that the BOJ did undertake such\par stealth \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month. It is being additionally fueled by the fact\par that the dollar seems to be garnering more support against the yen than\par against other key rivals.\par Japan's MOF declined comment. "It is a rumor and we cannot comment on that,"\par said Kuniyuki Hirai, special advisor to the chief representative for financial\par affairs at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in New York. Finance ministry official in\par Tokyo couldn't be reached for comment. No traders consulted for this report\par had actually seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par There has been speculation of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but I haven't seen clear\par evidence," said Toshiyuki Suzuki, chief economist at UFJ Bank in New York.\par Still, there were "some pretty credible... rumors out of Tokyo last night that\par they're leaning on the bid," said Robert Sinche, head of global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategy at Citibank in New York, referring to efforts to sell the yen by the\par finance ministry.\par "Certainly from the meetings we had in Tokyo last week, it seems as though\par there's a new approach to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," one that focuses on a more covert\par strategy, Sinche said.\par That break with the BOJ's previous habit of announcing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as and\par when they occur has made traders more trigger happy to seize on speculation,\par even though on the eve of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations\par meeting, some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategists don't think such action likely. G7 finance\par ministers and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governors are set to meet Friday and Saturday in\par Paris.\par Nonetheless, traders' suspicion was fueled by a strong warning from a Japanese\par official earlier in Thursday's session, indicating that the finance ministry\par is prepared to act in order to stem a sharp appreciation of the yen.\par Japanese institutions, perhaps encouraged by the MOF, have been buying the\par dollar against the yen when the dollar has slipped to levels between Y118.30\par and Y118.60 earlier in the global session, said David Leaver, senior trader\par with Gain Capital in Warren, N.J.\par Others expressed more skepticism that the Japanese government would act\par directly in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market just ahead of newly confirmed Treasury\par Secretary John Snow's debut at the G7 meeting. Snow has indicated that he\par doesn't approve of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par "Actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the eve of the G7 meeting, when covert \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at\par the end of January was criticized, would be a slap in the face to the other G7\par members," said Marc Chandler, chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with HSBC in New York.\par The BOJ could have been in the market, but it is more likely that the "fear of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  working could do the trick," and that is what is slowing the\par yen's rise, Chandler said\par Midmorning Thursday, the dollar wasn't far off global session lows. Against\par the yen, the dollar was at Y118.4 right in the area where some traders had\par cited suspicions of Japanese institutions buying dollars on the finance\par ministry's behalf and down moderately from Y118.63 late Wednesday in New York.\par The euro was at $1.0790, up from $1.0756 late Wednesday. Against the Swiss\par franc, the dollar was at CHF1.3615, down from CHF1.3668 late Wednesday.\par Sterling was at $1.5950, down from $1.5973.\par    By John Parry and Tyler Lifton; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par    tyler.lifton@dowjones.com; 201-938-2248\par Copyright 2003 OsterDowJones Commodity News (ODJ). All rights reserved.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 02-20-03 1200ET\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020030220dz2k00k2j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
