\par\par \b \uc2  Traders Fear Covert  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  May Be Braking Yen Rise \b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry and Tyler Lifton \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 16:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The suspicion that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is helping to support the dollar against the yen Thursday morning in New York, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and strategists said. \par \par \uc2  This shadow of a doubt that the Bank of Japan, which acts on behalf of the finance ministry, may be actively involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to weaken the yen, is being stoked by the fact that the BOJ did undertake such stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month. It is being additionally fueled by the fact that the dollar seems to be garnering more support against the yen than against other key rivals. \par \par \uc2  Japan's MOF declined comment. "It is a rumor and we cannot comment on that," said Kuniyuki Hirai, special advisor to the chief representative for financial affairs at  the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York. Finance ministry official in Tokyo couldn't be reached for comment. No traders consulted for this report had actually seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  There has been speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but I haven't seen clear evidence," said Toshiyuki Suzuki, chief economist at UFJ Bank in New York. \par \par \uc2  Still, there were "some pretty credible... rumors out of Tokyo last night that they're leaning on the bid," said Robert Sinche, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Citibank in New York, referring to efforts to sell the yen by the finance ministry. \par \par \uc2  "Certainly from the meetings we had in Tokyo last week,  it seems as though there's a new approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one that focuses on a more covert strategy, Sinche said. \par \par \uc2  That break with the BOJ's previous habit of announcing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as and when they occur has made traders more trigger happy to seize on speculation, even though on the eve of the Group of Seven leading industrial nations meeting, some \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists don't think such action likely. G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors are set to meet Friday and Saturday in Paris. \par \par \uc2  Nonetheless, traders' suspicion was fueled by a strong warning from a Japanese official earlier in Thursday's session, indicating that the finance ministry is prepared to  act in order to stem a sharp appreciation of the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japanese institutions, perhaps encouraged by the MOF, have been buying the dollar against the yen when the dollar has slipped to levels between Y118.30 and Y118.60 earlier in  the global session, said David Leaver, senior trader with Gain Capital in Warren, N.J. \par \par \uc2  Others expressed more skepticism that the Japanese government would act directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market  just ahead of newly confirmed Treasury Secretary John Snow's debut at the G7 meeting. Snow has indicated that he doesn't approve of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the eve of the G7 meeting, when  covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of January was criticized, would be a slap in the face to the other G7 members," said Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with HSBC in New York. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ could have been in the market, but it is more likely that the "fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  working could do the trick," and that is what is slowing the yen's rise, Chandler said \par \par \uc2  Midmorning Thursday, the dollar wasn't far off global session lows. Against the yen, the dollar was at Y118.4 right in the area where some traders had cited suspicions of  Japanese institutions buying dollars on the finance ministry's behalf and down moderately from Y118.63 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0790, up from $1.0756 late Wednesday.  Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at CHF1.3615, down from CHF1.3668 late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.5950, down  from $1.5973. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    By John Parry and Tyler Lifton; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par    tyler.lifton@dowjones.com; 201-938-2248\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020030220dz2k005v5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
