\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar on defensive in Asia as war fears weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 00:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The dollar tottered near a three-week low against the yen in early Asian dealings on Thursday on the re-emergence of risks of war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Investors have sold the dollar on concerns that the United States could launch a unilateral military offensive against Iraq without the sanction of the United Nations. \par \par \uc2  Those fears have been amplified as Washington has tried without success to win the backing of reluctant allies for military action. \par \par \uc2  By 2316 GMT, the dollar traded at 118.66/74 yen compared to 118.70 in late New York trade and not far from a three-week low of 118.57 yen hit overnight. \par \par \uc2  The euro was flat at $1.0745/48 from $1.0745 and at 127.50/62 Y 127.55. \par \par \uc2  Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be swayed by risks of an unloading in heavy euro positions, especially in the euro/yen cross. \par \par \uc2  "Japanese investors, depending on where domestic stocks are trading at the beginning of March, will need to take profits in something before March bookclosings (for the end of Japan's financial year), and that could well be in euro-denominated assets," said a trader at a foreign bank. \par \par \uc2  But many doubted the yen would draw much strength after fresh warnings on Wednesday from Japanese officials, who worry that its strength could crimp exports. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently admitted it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen in late January, and many wondered if such action would be discussed at a Group of Seven meeting in Paris this weekend. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Treasury undersecretary for international affairs, John Taylor, said on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely feature in discussions in meetings of finance ministers, though it would not be the main focus of the talks. \par \par \uc2  This appeared to contradict statements by Japanese and Canadian officials that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be on the G7 agenda. \par \par \uc2  Data on Wednesday showing the U.S. housing sector remaining buoyant in January failed to help both Wall Street and the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...        Debt...      Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030219dz2j02289\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
