\par\par \b \uc2  Yen down as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  keeps  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat alive. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2003\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 19 (Reuters) - The yen slipped on Wednesday as Japanese authorities repeated their mantra that they were watching market moves and would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  jumped. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said the yen's jump to a 2-= week high on the dollar and a three-week peak against the euro on Tuesday had been "a bit rapid". \par \par \uc2  "We will closely watch market moves and take action if needed," Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters. \par \par \uc2  His comments put to rest speculation in some quarters of the market overnight that Japan had quit its campaign to stamp out an export-crimping rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Such talk had emerged after Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  values would not be discussed at an upcoming Group of Seven (G7) meeting, a call some thought was due to a reluctance to offend other countries with manipulation in the market. \par \par \uc2  But with Japan's top government spokesman also saying the government was watching the yen's rise closely, Tokyo traders were left to conclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat remained. \par \par \uc2  Some even cited vague talk of dollar bids from authorities, though noting that such talk had turned into near-daily fare after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently admitted it had had kept quiet about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last month. \par \par \uc2  "The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still there, and with Mizoguchi's comment this morning, it is too risky to assume that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the G7 meeting," said Shogo Nagaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Trust and Banking. \par \par \uc2  By late afternoon, the dollar traded at 119.03/06 yen off an earlier low of 118.87 and higher than a late New York level of 118.96. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar between 118-119 yen is already an alert level for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mitsuru Sahara, vice president of UFJ Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealing group. \par \par \uc2  "There is no yen-buying factor to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up from the current level, and the possibility looms that there will be no (U.S.) attack in Iraq," he said. \par \par \uc2  BRACING FOR IRAQ \par \par \uc2  Traders said position adjustments in the euro were also on pause given uncertainty over whether the United States would forge ahead with war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The euro was up at $1.0732/35 from $1.0687 in late U.S. trading. Against the Japanese unit, it held at 127.66/76 yen after getting trounced to a three-week low of 126.95 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Yesterday's losses in dollar/yen and euro/yen were just a result of adjustments in positions, and it should be temporary," said Nagaya at Nomura Trust. \par \par \uc2  Some were said to be paring positions in the euro on the view that the immediate threat of war with Iraq had receded. \par \par \uc2  But many were doubtful after U.S. President George W. Bush insisted that mass peace protests around the world last weekend had not blunted his determination to disarm Iraq by force if necessary, either with or without a new U.N. resolution. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...        Debt...      Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030219dz2j00eif\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
