\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen jumps on Japan's G7 comments, US coupon talk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2003\par 10:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Feb 18 (Reuters) - The yen set two-week highs on the dollar and three-week peaks versus the euro on Tuesday as Tokyo said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be discussed at this weekend's G7 meeting, easing concern about imminent yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sizeable yen buying from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  fanned talk that investors were repatriating U.S. Treasury coupon payments due this week. Some banks estimate several billion worth of dollars could be exchanged into yen this week. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the dollar/yen exchange rate would not be slated for discussion when he meets his U.S. counterpart on the sidelines of the G7 meeting in Paris this weekend. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa's comments grabbed the headlines as the market has been alert to Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy ahead of the appointment of the next Bank of Japan governor and talk of drastic policy to reflate the economy," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Halifax Bank of Scotland Treasury Services. \par \par \uc2  "There was underlying yen-positive flows on coupon payments although this is likely to dissipate over the course of the week." \par \par \uc2  By 0910 GMT the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had gained nearly a full yen to a two-week high of 119.08 to the dollar from late New York on Monday. Against the euro it had risen one percent to to 127.63. \par \par \uc2  Japan is expected to name a successor to BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, whose five-year terms ends on March 19, soon. Shiokawa and Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi both said on Tuesday however that the government made no decision yet. \par \par \uc2  SENSITIVE TO POLICY \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi also said he does not see any need for discussion of exchange rates at this weekend. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say these comments lessened the possibility of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Tokyo and Washington when the dollar weakened rapidly. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers also said Japanese investors were selling U.S. Treasuries and converting the proceeds into yen before the business year ends on March 31, a move seen every year as companies try to dress up their books. \par \par \uc2  "In preparation for book closings, investors including banks are most likely taking profits in U.S. Treasuries as war now seems to have been postponed for a while and due to caution about any surprise at the G7 meeting this weekend," said Yasuhiro Miyata, manager at Dai-ichi Mutual Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Bank estimated the U.S. Treasury is due to make total coupon payments of $24.64 billion this week. It said Japanese investors hold approximately 11 percent of Treasuries though a breakdown by individual issue is not available. \par \par \uc2  But the bank's analysts played down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact of these coupon flows, saying informed market participants might at least partially hedge this known flow ahead of time. \par \par \uc2  SENTIMENT TEST \par \par \uc2  War concerns proved to be a drag for the dollar with uncertainties remaining about whether the United States will lead an attack on Iraq without the support of its major European allies. \par \par \uc2  Late on Monday the 15 leaders of the European Union delivered a joint warning to Iraq that force could be used as a last resort, but they remained split on the key issues of how long arms inspections should continue. \par \par \uc2  The euro was not without its problems, with investors anxiously awaiting the release of the German ZEW index which is set to show a deterioration in German economic sentiment. \par \par \uc2  The index, due at 1000 GMT, is expected to slip to 6.9 in February from 14 the month before when it rose for the first time in seven months. \par \par \uc2  A larger than expected fall in the index would further cement the view that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would cut rates as early as March. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030218dz2i00ity\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
