\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Rises Vs Yen As Japanese Banks Buy \b0\par\par\uc2  By Ron Harui \par \uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2003\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar rose slightly against the yen in Asia Monday as buying from Japanese commercial banks overcame profit-taking by interbank players in the U.S. holiday-thinned market. \par \par \uc2  Driven by dollar demand from corporate customers such as importers, Japanese banks bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in the session, pushing the dollar to an intraday high of Y120.78 at the 0100 GMT Tokyo fixing. \par \par \uc2  But the greenback soon succumbed to profit-taking by players reluctant to hold on to their dollar-long positions against the backdrop of ongoing geopolitical concerns, knocking the dollar back down to the mid-Y120s. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's focus on fresh developments in the Iraq situation is unchanged, but players will also closely watch the meeting of Group of Seven finance officials this weekend and a possible announcement next week of the new leadership team at the Bank of Japan, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar could consolidate in a Y119-Y122 range this week" ahead of those events, said a Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  At this weekend's meeting, finance ministers and central bankers from the G7 leading industrialized nations are expected to discuss the global economies and the impact on them and the financial markets if a war in Iraq breaks out. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, however, are likely to pay more attention to any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related comments emerging from a meeting between U.S. Treasury Secretary John Snow and Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa at the G7, especially after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. \par \par \uc2  Another eagerly awaited event is Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's selection of replacements for the outgoing BOJ governor and deputy governors. Current governor Masaru Hayami and deputy governors Sakuya Fujiwara and Yutaka Yamaguchi are scheduled to retire March 19. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y120.47, above Y120.30 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y120.41 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0722, lower than $1.0794 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.0835 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y129.16, down from Y129.85 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y130.48 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  As part of the Japanese government's efforts to put the nation's economy firmly on a recovery path, Koizumi is expected to appoint a BOJ leadership team committed to fighting prolonged deflation with aggressive steps such as further quantitative easing. This would act to weaken the yen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But, other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders argue that three deflation fighters at the helm of the BOJ may not be able to overcome opposition from the majority of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board members to radical easing measures. \par \par \uc2  "Consequently, any weakening of the yen from such an announcement by Koizumi may be short-lived," said another Tokyo dealer. \par \par \uc2  However, some observers speculate that Koizumi may nominate former BOJ deputy governor Toshihiko Fukui as the next BOJ governor, favoring reliability and consistency over deflation-fighting. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market still relatively long euros against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some speculators sold euros for dollars and for yen to take profits, dragging both \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs lower in the Asian session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The speculator-led sales and triggering of stop-loss sales orders in the low to mid-$1.0700s pushed the euro down around 65 pips to near the psychologically important level of $1.0700 and drove the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down to around the Y129 level. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6071, down from $1.6142 in New York and lower than $1.6216 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2942; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030217dz2h0009m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
