\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Falls Vs Euro, Yen; Blix Report Fears \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Twaronite \par \uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2003\par 06:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar lost ground against both the yen and the euro in Asia Thursday on fears of what chief U.N. weapons inspector Hans Blix might reveal in his Friday report. \par \par \uc2  Those fears were heightened by news that international missile experts have found that an Iraqi missile system exceeds the maximum 150-kilometer range allowed under U.N. resolutions. \par \par \uc2  The dollar lost ground against the euro as U.S. funds took advantage of relatively thin Tokyo lunchtime conditions to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against both the euro and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as $1.0765 but fell back on profit-taking after failing to clear resistance at $1.0770. \par \par \uc2  The rise wasn't "a particularly euro-driven phenomenon," says J.P. Morgan strategist James Malcolm, but was clearly the result of dollar selling against both the euro and the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  Against the Swiss franc, the dollar retreated from an early high of $1.3719 to a low of $1.3644 in tandem with the euro's rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's losses against the yen were limited by both persistent concerns about Japan's economic fundamentals and fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take action to stem the yen's rise ahead of the end of the nation's fiscal year next month. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Zembei Mizoguchi, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, made it clear Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if concerns over a looming Iraq conflict precipitate any yen rise against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Noting that worries about Iraq could upset markets, Mizoguchi said the ministry was watching the situation "very closely" and would take appropriate steps against volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y120.95, below Y121.27 in New York, but above Y120.82 in Tokyo late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0751, higher than $1.0715 in New York and $1.0749 in Tokyo. Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y130.03, compared with Y129.94 in New York and Y129.85 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Market participants still fear that Japanese authorities could conduct "stealth" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, as they did in January. \par \par \uc2  Since the MOF on Jan. 31 confirmed those actions, traders have speculated as to whether the ministry has carried out any more such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Data Thursday underscored exactly why MOF thinks \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs the tail wind of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster its economy. \par \par \uc2  A Cabinet Office survey showed Japanese companies cut their capital expenditures a seasonally adjusted 0.7% in the October-December period from the previous quarter. The fall follows a 3.1% increase in the July-September quarter and suggests that Japan's fragile export-led recovery has stalled. \par \par \uc2  The decline raises expectations that October-December gross domestic product data will show a contraction. Economists expect GDP figures, scheduled for release at 0850 local time Friday morning in Tokyo, to show that the economy shrank by 0.3% on quarter in real terms, compared to 0.8% growth in the previous period. \par \par \uc2  While a much better-than-expected figure could weigh on the dollar against the yen, "it's amazing how little anyone's watching the GDP figures this time with Iraq on everyone's mind," said a trader at a U.S. brokerage. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6185, up from $1.6158 in New York, but lower than $1.6193 in Tokyo Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Lisa Twaronite, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; lisa.twaronite@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030213dz2d000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
