\par\par \b \uc2  G7 to focus on risks from Iraq war-Japan official. \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2003\par 12:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 12 (Reuters) - Talks about how to shield the global economy from the impact of a possible war in Iraq will be at the forefront of this month's Group of Seven meeting in Paris, a Japanese official said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  But the G7 leading economies had no plans yet for any specific coordinated action, said Hiroshi Watanabe, the head of the Japanese Finance Ministry international bureau. \par \par \uc2  "During broad economic surveillance (review) discussions there will be talks about how the economy can withstand the impact if something happens," Watanabe told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "But there are no explicit plans that I know of to discuss what specifically to do in fiscal or monetary policy." \par \par \uc2  He played down talk that Germany could expand fiscal spending, saying he knew of no such plan and that even if there was one it was probably more a domestic issue. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from G7 countries - Britain, Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan and the United States - are due to meet in Paris on February 21-22. \par \par \uc2  Compared with the last meeting in Washington in September, where support for developing countries and debt relief were the major topics, more focus should be given to talks on conditions in the world economy, or economic surveillance, Watanabe said. \par \par \uc2  "Economic surveillance will be a big part of the discussions," he said. "I don't know if it will be the most important topic, but it will certainly be in focus. \par \par \uc2  Watanabe said North Korea's heightened rhetoric over its nuclear policy was a major risk for Japan as a nation, but that it was less important than Iraq in terms of economic impact. \par \par \uc2  He also said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates would, as usual, be part of the discussions, although they were unlikely to be at the top of the agenda. \par \par \uc2  He said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plans to bring up the yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it conducted last week at the G7 meeting unless asked to explain. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said earlier this month that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  discreetly on its behalf in the market from mid-January, spending about $6 billion to buy dollars for yen in a move it said was aimed at stabilising the yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030212dz2c00n0a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
