\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Hemmed In Vs Yen; Mkt Dulled To War Risks \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Soble \par \uc2 686 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2003\par 06:42\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar stayed pinned in a tight range against the yen in another anemic Asian session Monday, as the U.S. unit looked increasingly immune to the geopolitical risks that have dogged it for months. \par \par \uc2  In a pattern that's become familiar in recent sessions, the dollar was underpinned by the specter of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry, and by a sense that the market has factored in most of the downside risk from a potential war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  "It's becoming harder to sell dollars - though that doesn't mean there's a reason to buy dollars either," said Shuji Takano, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Aozora Bank. \par \par \uc2  With specific Iraq-related trading incentives scarce, at least for now, talk among Tokyo traders focused on an issue closer to home: the identity of the next Bank of Japan governor. \par \par \uc2  Some expected the name of Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's choice to replace outgoing governor Masaru Hayami to emerge later this week, when Koizumi meets with leaders of his ruling coalition. \par \par \uc2  The dollar could rise "as much as Y5" if Koizumi picks an advocate of radical monetary easing, said Toru Umemoto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Morgan Stanley in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The official announcement of Hayami's replacement will likely take more time, however. \par \par \uc2  Japan's chief government spokesman said Monday the appointment may not come until after the Group of Seven meeting of finance ministers and central bankers February 21-22 in Paris. \par \par \uc2  "We can't really go (to the G7 meeting) carrying a sign that says this (\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief) will change soon," said Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda. \par \par \uc2  Hayami's term ends March 19. Koizumi has been saying he will nominate a new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head around Feb. 20. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT, the dollar was quoted at Y120.31, above Y120.24 late Friday in New York. The dollar was at Y119.75 late Friday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0818, lower than $1.0831 late Friday in New York. The euro was at $1.0811 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y130.15, down slightly from Y130.23 in New York late Friday. The euro was at Y129.46 in Tokyo late Friday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6311, down from $1.6317 in New York and $1.6346 in Tokyo Friday. \par \par \uc2  Underscoring the market's less pessimistic view on the dollar, the latest data from the Chicago Mercantile Exchange's International Money Market showed net yen-long positions - speculative bets against the dollar for the yen - plunged 78% last week, to 5,594 contracts from 25,610 contracts in the week ended Jan. 28. \par \par \uc2  Net long bets on the yen now stand at their lowest level since the week to December 24, Morgan Stanley analysts said in a research note. \par \par \uc2  The timing of the sharp drop suggests short-term speculators rushed to unwind yen longs after the Finance Ministry revealed January 31 that it secretly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen several times in the month. \par \par \uc2  Since the announcement, rumors have circulated in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets that the MOF has ordered several more covert \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Ministry officials have refused to comment, but it's clear their cloak-and-dagger approach has kept the market on its toes. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , real or imagined, is very much a factor," said a trader at a Japanese bank. "As long as the MOF seems to be drawing a line of defense below Y120, there's not much anyone who wants to sell the dollar can do." \par \par \uc2  -By Jonathan Soble, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; jonathan.soble@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  The chart of late Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates that accompanied Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been replaced with an enhanced \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixture that is updated hourly. \par \par \uc2  Subscribers can find this table: \par \par \uc2  -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087. \par \par \uc2  -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX \par \par \uc2  -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT \par \par \uc2  -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030210dz2a0009e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
