\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar holds soft tone, bows to war uncertainty. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2003\par 07:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 4 (Reuters) - The dollar held a soft tone in Asia on Tuesday, failing to make the most of good U.S. manufacturing data as it bowed to worries about chances of war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  Eking out a small advance in midday Asian trade, the dollar soon reversed course as traders cited a general apathy to trade actively ahead of a speech by U.S. Secretary of State Colin Powell to the U.N. Security Council on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Powell will present the U.S. case that Iraq is hiding banned weapons from U.N. arms inspectors, and the event is seen as a key test of whether the United States can can drum up support from wary allies for a military strike against Baghdad. \par \par \uc2  Most players think a unilateral attack by the United States would bode ill for the greenback. \par \par \uc2  "There isn't any reason to buy the dollar now, but likewise there is no reason to build up yen positions," said Koichi Abe, manager at Aozora Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading section. \par \par \uc2  The dollar drew some support after the Institute for Supply Management said U.S. manufacturing expanded in January for the third straight month, and at a faster-than-expected pace. \par \par \uc2  Still, sentiment was clouded by war fears and structural risks in the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  "It's going to take some time for the dollar to get over geopolitical risks as well as fundamental negatives like the U.S. trade and budget deficits," said Daisuke Uno, chief market analyst at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp. \par \par \uc2  By 0617 GMT, the dollar was at 120.18/21 yen from 120.28 in late New York and a 1 = month high of 120.93 on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was supported at $1.0775/78 from $1.0769. Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 129.47/59 yen after a failed attempt to clear 130 yen, a key options level. \par \par \uc2  GEOPOLITICAL TENSIONS WEIGH \par \par \uc2  The yen was looking limp after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's revelation last week that it had covertly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January. Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a warning measure. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a European bank said: "The dollar's downside (against the yen) is becoming more limited due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but heavy resistance is also seen around 121 yen." \par \par \uc2  With the focus squarely on U.S.-related factors, traders said it would be a while before the market turned to negatives on Japan, such as the usual worries over its financial sector at the end of the fiscal year in March. \par \par \uc2  "There's still uncertainty on the dollar, whether a possible war in Iraq may drag on or whether the start of conflict will be delayed, even though it may not turn out so," said Uno at Sumitomo Mitsui. \par \par \uc2  Some traders were also paying attention to news that U.S. forces have been put on alert for a possible movement near North Korea. \par \par \uc2  U.S. defence officials said on Monday that U.S. bombers, fighter jets and warships have been alerted for possible deployment to the western Pacific to deter any aggression by North Korea in case of a war in Iraq. \par \par \uc2  But the officials told Reuters that U.S. Defense Secretary Donald Rumsfeld had not issued any final orders to move B-52 bombers, F-16 fighter jets or naval units. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  All \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news ...        Debt...      Indicators...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par  Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par  Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030204dz2400cib\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
