\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar on rollercoaster as Koizumi denies BOJ gov report. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Kazunori Takada \par \uc2 705 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2003\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The dollar spiked more than one yen against the yen on Monday morning after a Japanese news agency said Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi was considering appointing a supporter of inflation targeting as Bank of Japan governor. \par \par \uc2  Kyodo news agency cited ruling Liberal Democratic Party sources as saying Koizumi had agreed that Nakahara, a former BOJ board member, was the best choice to replace BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, whose term expires in March. \par \par \uc2  But Koizumi denied the report, saying the decision was still a "blank sheet of paper." \par \par \uc2  The dollar gained some 0.3 yen immediately after the Kyodo report, then rose by a fall yen before erasing its gains following Koizumi's comments to reporters. \par \par \uc2  Many traders say the appointment of Nakahara, an advocate of inflation targeting as well as foreign bond buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would be negative for the yen. \par \par \uc2  Senior politicians have called on the BOJ to adopt inflation targeting as a way to overcome deflation, but Hayami has rejected it as a reckless gamble. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had earlier advanced against the yen and the euro in adding to gains made after better-than-expected U.S. manufacturing data and confirmation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As of 0312 GMT, the dollar was trading at 120.13/18 yen compared with 119.89 in late pre-weekend trade. It briefly hit a high of 120.93. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0745/50 compared with $1.0761, and was at 129.07/24 yen against 129.03. \par \par \uc2  But traders said the long-term outlook remained bearish for the greenback as Iraqi war fears continued to linger. \par \par \uc2  A key event for the market this week will be U.S. Secretary of State Colin Powell's presentation of evidence to the U.N. Security Council on Wednesday which the U.S. says will show that Iraq has defied bans on weapons programmes. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar-selling trend has not changed," said Junya Tanase, global markets officer at JP Morgan Chase. "But against the yen, people will get cautious if it falls greatly." \par \par \uc2  On Friday, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it had covertly sold yen for dollars after mid-January to prevent its strength from dousing demand for exports and undercutting a fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A ministry official said it bought $6 billion worth of dollars on several occasions, confirming rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had helped keep the dollar underpinned in recent sessions. \par \par \uc2  COVERT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "I think 117.50 yen will become a key level," said J.P. Morgan's Tanase. Though MOF has not disclosed levels at which it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders speculated it was around 117 or 118 yen. \par \par \uc2  Top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi said on Monday that massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was possible if there were rapid movements in exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  But he added that any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be to prevent fluctuations, not to guide the yen lower. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be to guide the yen lower but to prevent fluctuations," Mizoguchi told reporters. \par \par \uc2  In recent years, the ministry has immediately confirmed when it has stepped into the market, and the amounts involved usually resulted in sharp moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, but traders said the covert action proved effective. \par \par \uc2  "Since the dollar/yen is now around 120 yen from 117 or 118 in mid-January when they were seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think you can say that the action did have an effect," said Motoshi Imura, senior manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and treasury at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi \par \par \uc2  "I think this (the convert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is a sign that Japanese authorities are becoming more flexible to market movements." \par \par \uc2  "This is prompting large-scale position adjustments, and if such flows also push up other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I think the dollar/yen could push up higher," Imura added. \par \par \uc2  On the economic data front, traders were awaiting more clues on the U.S. economy this week, with the Institute of Supply Management's January manufacturing index due on Monday and jobs data due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Economists expected the ISM manufacturing index to creep down to 53.0 after an upwardly revised December result of 55.2. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030203dz23005po\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of fina